From b6e5a08f24cba9f73143f99d92104094d10bd8d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sagi Shahar <sagis@google.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Jun 2024 01:37:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 74/86] KVM: selftests: TDX: Add TDX CPUID TDVMCALL test

This test issues a CPUID TDVMCALL from inside the guest to get the CPUID
values as seen by KVM.

Co-developed-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Sagi Shahar <sagis@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ackerley Tng <ackerleytng@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Afranji <afranji@google.com>
---
- Reinette: Squash fix from Isaku to fix verify_td_cpuid_tdcall().
  Because CPUID array was masked on creation, the value to guest is also
  masked.  Update tests to reflect it. Add attribution.

- Reinette: Remove "Change-Id:" tag.

- Reinette: Squash fixup from Adrian to use vcpu->cpuid for reference
  instead of kvm_get_supported_cpuid(). In particular, if KVM attempts to
  maintain a maximal guest CR4 value, then the CPUID runtime updates will
  have altered CPUID for OSXSAVE.

- Reinette: checkpatch.pl fixes: alignment should match open parenthesis,
  don't use multiple blank lines

- Reinette: switch to reverse fir where practical

- Reinette: Use vcpu_get_cpuid_entry() to avoid stale data per commit
  "KVM: selftests: Refresh vCPU CPUID cache in __vcpu_get_cpuid_entry()".
  Drop masking of CPUID bits now that the vCPU's CPUID bits are more
  accurate after switch to use KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID as baseline that already
  filtering.
