From bfd60fb1160ea6738bc09a675c65a7d073b8f764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Afranji <afranji@google.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Jun 2024 01:59:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 78/86] KVM: selftests: TDX: Add shared memory test

Adds a test that sets up shared memory between the host and guest.

Co-developed-by: Binbin Wu <binbin.wu@linux.intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Binbin Wu <binbin.wu@linux.intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Afranji <afranji@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Sagi Shahar <sagis@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ackerley Tng <ackerleytng@google.com>
---
- Yan: rebased to tdx_kvm_dev-2024-06-21

- Reinette: Rebase on top of fixup to "KVM: selftests: TDX: Add
  report_fatal_error test" that removed handle_userspace_tdg_vp_vmcall_exit()
  due to handling of TDG_VP_VMCALL_REPORT_FATAL_ERROR no longer needed.
  Bring handle_userspace_tdg_vp_vmcall_exit() back to match original
  behavior to support original handling of TDG_VP_VMCALL_MAP_GPA.

- Reinette: Squash fix from Binbin to request KVM_HC_MAP_GPA_RANGE to
  exit to userspace for handling via KVM_CAP_EXIT_HYPERCALL and obtain
  needed parameters from returned hypercall arguments to call
  handle_memory_conversion() directly.
  For reference, KVM patches:
     KVM: x86: Check hypercall's exit to userspac
     KVM: TDX: Handle TDG.VP.VMCALL<MapGPA>
  Add attribution.

- Reinette: Remove "Change-Id:" tag.

- Reinette: Squash fix from Adrian that use pre-calculated shared bit
  position instead of basing it on pa_bits because pa_bits can be
  different.  Note that the shared bit position is tested elsewhere so
  this test does not need to test it too.

- Reinette: checkpatch.pl fixes: alignment should match open parenthesis,
  comparison to NULL could be written "test_mem_hva",
  lines should not end with a '('. Also remove kerneldoc marker ("/**")
  from comment that does not use kerneldoc formatting.

- Reinette: Squash fix from Isaku that quiets handle_memory_conversion() by
  using pr_debug() instead of printf(). It's too noisy to use printf() on
  every handle_memory_conversion() call.

- Reinette: switch to reverse fir where practical

- Reinette: add vCPU ID as parameter to handle_memory_conversion() to
  support debugging of MMU stress tests that manipulate memory from
  multiple vCPUs and host.
